<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Vienna (1529)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1529">1529</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-habsburg-wars">Ottoman–Habsburg wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1529 was the first Ottoman attempt to capture the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> capital, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>. Bad weather, long supply lines and a determined defence forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> to withdraw. Accounts of the Ottoman Empire place it among Suleiman's major campaigns, marking the limit of Ottoman expansion in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
